<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<QuickAction xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT MUST SIT INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT. A comment placed ABOVE <QuickAction>
        breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with the misleading error "unable to find
        matching parent xml file". Precedent: Broker_Protection_Access.permissionset-meta.xml.

        DISPOSITION LOI ONLY. The other half of the sell-side negotiation LOOP - read this
        together with LOI__c.Mark_Countered_By_DPEG, which carries the full rationale.

        THIS ACTION MOVES Countered by DPEG -> Counter Received from Buyer.

        ⚠ THAT EDGE IS ALSO THE LINEAR NEXT HOP, SO THIS BUTTON OVERLAPS Advance Stage AT THAT
        STAGE, AND THE OVERLAP IS DELIBERATE. Two reasons. (1) SYMMETRY: a user driving a loop
        should see the same shape of control at both of its stages; making one direction a
        named button and the other an anonymous "advance" invites the user to guess. (2)
        INDEPENDENCE: the linear NEXT_STAGE map for the disposition record type lives in
        RecordStageAdvanceService - the developer's file, not this one - and if a later change
        re-points the hop out of Countered by DPEG, a page that depended on Advance Stage for
        this edge would silently lose it. An explicit target cannot drift that way.
        The cost is one redundant button on one stage. Do not "tidy" it away without moving
        the loop's other edge somewhere it can be expressed, which today is nowhere.

        🔴 THE LWC BUNDLE IS NOT IN THIS TRANCHE'S DECLARATIVE SCOPE. The expected name is
        lwc/loiMarkCounterReceived. It is the developer's file. This quick action WILL FAIL
        DEPLOY until that bundle exists - deploy them together.

        🔴 IT ALSO NEEDS AN APEX ALLOW-LIST ENTRY: 'Counter Received from Buyer' added to the
        LOI DISPOSITION explicit-target set, record-type-scoped. Record-type picklist
        restriction is UI-ONLY and is NOT enforced by Apex DML.

        NAMING: the API name is Mark_Counter_Received rather than Mark_Counter_Received_From_
        Buyer purely for length; the LABEL carries the full stage wording, which is what a user
        sees. LOI__c.Mark_Countered already exists and is the ACQUISITION action (it sets
        Stage__c = 'Counter'); these two names are deliberately distinct from it and from each
        other so no future reader has to disambiguate three similar buttons by their labels.
    -->
    <actionSubtype>Action</actionSubtype>
    <label>Counter Received from Buyer</label>
    <lightningWebComponent>loiMarkCounterReceived</lightningWebComponent>
    <optionsCreateFeedItem>false</optionsCreateFeedItem>
    <type>LightningWebComponent</type>
</QuickAction>
